      "message": "perf(3d): facet grid for the drop-cutter support scan\n\nThe support facets of 3D finishing are now a SupSet: the facets plus a\nuniform XY bucket grid (CSR cells, Ericson ch. 7). The point scans\n(support_at, support_grad, ball_clear, column_clear, fold_best) read only\nthe facets of the cell that holds the query point. Each scan keeps its\nown padded-box reject, and each cell lists its facets in ascending index,\nso every answer has the same bits as the full scan.\n\nA non-finite box, a non-finite query or an extent that the grid cannot\nsize falls back to the full scan. SupSet::full_scan keeps the old scan as\nthe reference for the parity tests and for the GPU filter of #2526.\n\nPinned by grid_scan_matches_full_scan_on_bumps,\ngrid_scan_matches_full_scan_on_big_and_degenerate_facets,\ngrid_candidates_hold_every_facet_whose_box_holds_the_point and\nnon_finite_input_falls_back_to_the_full_scan.\n\nFixes #2619\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
